Hey, I'm a retired math teacher picking up programming for fun. Here's my edit-distance function in JavaScript. What's your take on it?
```js
function lev(a, b) {
  let prev = Array.from({ length: b.length + 1 }, (_, i) => i);
  for (let i = 1; i <= a.length; i++) {
    const cur = [i];
    for (let j = 1; j <= b.length; j++)
      cur[j] = Math.min(prev[j] + 1, cur[j-1] + 1, prev[j-1] + (a[i-1] !== b[j-1]));
    prev = cur;
  }
  return prev[b.length];
}
```

